A thin envelope lay on the dining table, untouched since it arrived early that morning. The wax seal was smooth to the touch but felt as heavy as a promise broken.

Elena carefully tore open the letter, her fingers shaking slightly despite herself. She never bothered to look at the address or return name—she knew who sent it long before reading the first word:

*"Dear Members of Our Community,"*

She read each line with growing unease. The letter spoke in measured tones, almost conversational but laced with a sinister undertone: *“Have you noticed how the night is always longer on your streets? How the shadows seem to stretch and grow every time you turn your back?"* 

It continued with subtle hints at threats, like a knife gliding near your neck—*“The wind that whistles through the alleys, whispering tales of those who came before. Do you let it guide you?”*

