She glanced towards her family—her children, sleeping peacefully in their rooms. The thought of anyone threatening them was unbearable. And yet, there it was—the unspoken threat hanging between every line: *“Learn to be wary at all times. Stay indoors before it’s too late.”*

Elena’s hands clasped tightly together as she unfolded the letter more completely. She needed help, but who could she trust now?

The envelope was closed again with trembling fingers, and Elena left the letter on the table where no one else would see, her mind racing with possibilities. There must be a way to protect them from this shadow without making herself a target.

